.TH CJSON_SERIALIZE_FREE_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_serialize_free_mp, cjson_serialize_free \- free a string returned by the serializer
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cjson.h>

void cjson_serialize_free_mp(char *s, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
/* convenience wrapper; default allocator */
static inline void cjson_serialize_free(char *s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees a string that cjson_serialize() or cjson_serialize_pretty()
returned.  mp must be the allocator that was given to
cjson_parse_mp() or cjson_create_*_mp() when the serialized tree was
built, or NULL when the tree used the default allocator.
cjson_serialize_free() is a static inline wrapper that calls
cjson_serialize_free_mp(s, NULL).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   The string to free, which may be NULL.
mp  The allocator that frees it, or NULL for the default allocator.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_serialize (3),
.BR cjson_serialize_pretty (3)
